---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Apple requires the support URL to "lead to actual contact information", so the email is
// the point of this page — everything else is here to answer the question before it's asked.
const email = 'support@mili.family';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wallchart — Support"
  description="Help for Wallchart, the tap-to-track habit widget for iPhone."
  noindex={true}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Wallchart</p>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and I'll read it. Include your iPhone model
      and iOS version if something is broken.
    </p>

    <h2>Adding the widget</h2>
    <p>
      The widget is the app. To add it: touch and hold an empty part of your Home Screen until
      the icons jiggle, tap <em>Edit</em> in the top-left, tap <em>Add Widget</em>, search for
      Wallchart, pick a size, and tap <em>Add Widget</em>. Tapping a habit on the widget logs it
      without opening the app.
    </p>

    <h2>The three sizes hold different amounts</h2>
    <p>
      Small shows three habits, medium four, large ten. If you have more habits than the widget
      can show, it lists as many as fit and says how many are hidden. Reorder your habits in the
      app — touch and hold a row and drag — to choose which ones make the cut.
    </p>

    <h2>Counters wrap back to zero</h2>
    <p>
      A counter habit counts up one per tap. Tapping it again once it has reached its goal starts
      the day over at zero, so one control can both add and reset. If you overshoot, keep tapping
      round to the number you want.
    </p>

    <h2>Days reset at midnight</h2>
    <p>
      Each day is stored separately, so a new day starts empty on its own — there is nothing to
      reset and nothing to remember. Past days are never overwritten. Tap a habit to open its
      history, then tap any past day on the calendar to correct it.
    </p>

    <h2>Archive keeps history, delete does not</h2>
    <p>
      Swiping a habit away archives it: it disappears from Today and the widget, and everything
      you logged is kept. <em>Delete Forever</em>, from the archived list, removes the habit and
      every day you ever logged for it. That one cannot be undone.
    </p>

    <h2>Sync to your own server</h2>
    <p>
      Optional, off until you fill it in, and meant for people who already run a server. Under
      <em>Settings → Sync to your own server</em>, enter a host and an access token and Wallchart
      will POST your habits and logged days to <code>https://your-host/api/sync</code> as you log
      them. <em>Restore from my server</em> pulls them back — useful on a new phone. Restore never
      overwrites a day this phone already has. On a phone with no habits of its own yet, your
      server's habits replace the starter examples.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you don't run a server, ignore this entirely. Wallchart is complete without it and sends
      nothing anywhere. See the <a href="/wallchart/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Nothing here answers it</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .prose :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }

  .prose :global(code) {
    font-family: 'Berkeley Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
  }
</style>
